  "Could you check the charge on my bill?": "您能帮我核对一下账单上的费用吗？",
  "This seems a practical starting point for both sides, subject to agreement.": "如果双方同意，这似乎是一个现实可行的起点。",
  "That is why I would favour this approach at this stage.": "这就是为什么在现阶段，我更倾向于采用这种做法。",
  "I would check this before promising an immediate solution to everyone involved.": "向所有相关人员承诺立即解决之前，我会先核实这一点。",
  "However, we should confirm the details carefully with everyone directly affected.": "不过，我们应该与所有直接受影响的人仔细确认细节。",
  "If that proves impractical, we should discuss another workable option together.": "如果事实证明这不可行，我们应该一起讨论其他可行方案。",
  "Could we clarify the main practical constraint before making a decision together?": "共同作出决定之前，我们能否先明确主要的实际限制？",
  "Let's review the actual outcome together rather than simply assume it worked.": "我们一起复核实际结果，而不要直接假定这种做法已经奏效。",
  "My assessment remains provisional at this stage.": "现阶段，我的评估仍是暂时性的。",
  "There are competing considerations to weigh carefully.": "有相互冲突的因素需要仔细权衡。",
  "The underlying assumptions matter to this decision.": "作出这个决定时，隐含的假设很重要。",
  "This recommendation has limits worth acknowledging explicitly.": "这项建议存在一些值得明确承认的局限。",
  "Several interests are at stake in this discussion.": "这场讨论涉及多方利益。",
  "A credible explanation needs scrutiny before we act.": "行动之前，即使是看似可信的解释，也需要仔细审查。",
  "The available evidence is incomplete in important respects.": "现有证据在一些重要方面仍不完整。",
  "Let's review the outcome together.": "我们一起复核结果吧。",
  "Alternative proposals remain welcome.": "我们仍然欢迎其他提议。",
  "Changed assumptions require reconsideration.": "假设发生变化，就需要重新考虑。",
  "The uncertainty should remain explicit.": "不确定性应该明确说明。",
  "Those interests deserve fair consideration.": "这些利益值得得到公平考虑。",
  "Unresolved objections should be recorded.": "尚未解决的反对意见应该记录下来。",
  "Please confirm responsibility for follow-up.": "请确认后续跟进由谁负责。",
  "I take your point, although I would be cautious about treating it as the whole picture.": "我理解您的观点，不过若把它当成全部情况，我会持谨慎态度。",
  "May I suggest a different way forward?": "我可以提出另一种推进办法吗？",
  "I am putting that forward for consideration, not presenting it as a decision already made.": "我提出这一点是供大家考虑，并不是说决定已经作出了。",
  "With respect, that conclusion goes a little further than the information supports.": "恕我直言，这个结论有些超出了现有信息能够支持的范围。",
  "I would welcome evidence that challenges that assessment.": "我愿意看到能够质疑这项评估的证据。",
  "I can accept the concern without accepting every proposed consequence.": "我可以认可这种担忧，但不一定接受由此提出的所有后果。",
  "That distinction matters if we want qualified agreement rather than reluctant compliance.": "如果我们希望获得有保留的同意，而不是勉强服从，这种区分就很重要。",
  "To be clear, I am proposing a next step, not promising a particular outcome.": "明确地说，我是在提出下一步行动，而不是承诺某个具体结果。",
  "Could we confirm that this is what we have agreed, and leave the unresolved points explicitly open?": "我们能否确认这是已经达成的一致，并明确保留尚未解决的问题？",
  "What would you recommend as a practical first response?": "您会建议采取什么切实可行的初步应对措施？",
  "How would you justify your preferred approach?": "您会如何说明自己倾向的做法有何依据？",
  "How would you make a careful proposal without implying a final decision?": "您会如何谨慎提出建议，而不暗示已经作出最终决定？",
  "How would you explain the wider point in natural language?": "您会如何用自然的语言解释更广泛的含义？",
  "How would you challenge an overconfident conclusion politely?": "您会如何礼貌地质疑一个过于自信的结论？",
  "How would you acknowledge the concern while limiting your agreement?": "您会如何承认对方的担忧，同时限定自己同意的范围？",
  "How would you close the discussion without overstating the agreement?": "您会如何结束讨论，而不过度表述双方已经达成的一致？",
  "We should review the resulting decision.": "我们应该复核由此作出的决定。",
  "I would rather clarify the implication than assume a commitment you have not made.": "我宁愿先澄清言外之意，也不愿假定您作出了尚未作出的承诺。",
  "Why did you decide to do that?": "你为什么决定这样做？",
  "What will you do if something similar happens?": "如果发生类似情况，你会怎么做？",
  "What was the main reason for your choice?": "你作出这个选择的主要原因是什么？",
  "How will you respond if your situation changes?": "如果情况改变，你会怎样应对？",
  "Could you explain what mattered to you?": "你能解释一下什么对你最重要吗？",
  "What is your plan for the next time?": "你下次有什么计划？",
  "What made that approach important to you?": "为什么这种做法对你很重要？",
  "What will you try if you face another problem like that?": "如果遇到另一个类似问题，你会尝试什么？",
  "Why did that seem like a useful step?": "为什么那似乎是一个有帮助的步骤？",
  "How do you plan to handle a similar situation?": "你打算怎样处理类似情况？"
}
